  "id": "COMPOUND:28471 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that (22R,25R)-spirosolan-3beta-ol may interact with SCCH-26 through a series of target relationships, with the most direct link being its interaction with Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This enzyme is targeted by (22R,25R)-spirosolan-3beta-ol, and in turn, it targets SCCH-26. Additionally, the compound is also linked to 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, which also targets SCCH-26. These findings suggest that (22R,25R)-spirosolan-3beta-ol may exert its biological effect by modulating the activity of a dehydrogenase/reductase enzyme, which in turn influences the behavior of SCCH-26. The evidence supports a mechanism where the compound acts as a target of a metabolic enzyme, potentially altering cellular processes in the SCCH-26 cell line. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for (22R,25R)-spirosolan-3beta-ol in modulating cellular metabolism, with SCCH-26 being a downstream target of multiple metabolic pathways.",
